>demon princes still have their own levels deep down so they would
>still be able to gate in fellow demons princes, but it sounds like
>regular unnamed demons can't gate the named princes just the
>two named lords?

Yes.

There is also one further way for demon princes to be summoned.  When
a wizardly monster casts "summon nasties" in Gehennom, there is a 10%
chance that instead of attempting to summon 1d(XL / 3) nasties, it
makes a single attempt to summon a demon (with a 1 in 4 chance of
summoning *two* demons of identical type if the selected demon is
non-unique) with no alignment constraints.

This demon-summoning attempt is made "as if by the Wizard of Yendor",
which is equivalent to it being made by a demon prince of no specified
alignment, yielding a 5% chance of a demon prince and a 23.75% chance of
a demon lord.
